 "tuning": "Fix round 3 (Nov 13, v4): the judges ruled mid b* and hi10 chroma grade-owned. 1-TR's mid b* (17.8) is low because a lavender sky (top band b* -10.9) sits beside orange grass (b* +31-37), not because its grass is pink; 1-TR's sunlit grass tips are paler (C 25) than its mid grass (C 44). v4 builds that split by luminance and chroma instead of one filter: `cool` turns the low-chroma upper mids (haze, cloud, sky, dust: L* 30-62, chroma < 14-28) lavender (x0.3 + (5, -20)); `mid` turns the warm mids (hue 52-100) toward orange with a* x1.38 / b* x0.84, -8 deg, sparing saturated cloth (cRange 38-54); `high` takes the lit band (L* 48-74, under the fire cores) to pale gold (chroma x0.36, +18 deg toward gold); `shadow` keeps rose-violet darks (+7, -5, x1.25). A new set `sunset` (18:30-19:12, between golden and dusk) carries the later, rosier light (mids b* x0.5 over hue 35-100, cool x0.3 + (7, -16), lit band +20 deg); `dusk` turns the dark mids violet (b* x0.05, -26 deg; shadows +12, -15.5) while firelit ground keeps its orange (cRange 26-42). toneC back to [15, 45, 0.5] (a stronger lift on saturated highlights cost fire chroma in the gamut map). Probes (HDR through the output at 17:45, W0 / v3 / v4): fire dim C 45 / 45 / 40, fire glow 18 / 18 / 18, orange shirt hue 49 / 47 / 46, firelit ground C 47 / 46 / 42. History: v3 (fix round 2) cut v2's rose-brown filter (near-neutral top band only, warm highlights x1.22, gamut-mapped lift); v2 (fix round 1) the first L*a*b* stage.",
